{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/912086-old-meets-new-sidhe-houses-as-entitlements","id":912086,"title":"Old Meets New - Sidhe Houses as Entitlements","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-10T21:51:38-07:00","id":912086,"title":"Old Meets New - Sidhe Houses as Entitlements","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hello all. I\u2019ve been poking at this idea as a thought experiment ever since the 2e playtest doc started floating around, and have recently decided to implement it in the 2e iteration of the online game I am on staff for (there\u2019s a link in my signature, if you\u2019re curious &lt;/shameless plug&gt;). I\u2019m working out the kinks mechanically, though, and that\u2019s why I\u2019m here.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The freehold will have two main courts pulled from the old Dreaming split of Seelie and Unseelie, with the Seelie holding power in the spring and summer and the Unseelie in autumn and winter. The Sidhe Houses would be represented by Court of Solstice-style entitlements that come with a different court emotion and a bonus flavored by the old house bonus in most cases. Membership in one of these Houses will grant the Lost a more \u2018noble\u2019 stature in the freehold than those who did not join a House or went with one of the cannon entitlements instead.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The rough draft of the sidhe house entitlements can be found <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11_J5J1qmvKEpZNmZ8k3kKnKIMa0rWLZU3aPnyTDpTX8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. The goals for the bonuses are roughly up to four dots of merits, either in merit dots or mechanics tied to the old house boons. Let me know what you think, and I\u2019ll happily take any suggestions you have to offer.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Pay no attention to the man behind the Storyteller!&quot; <hr /><a href=\"https://www.fromdusktilljawn.com/\" target=\"_blank\">From Dusk 'til Jawn</a> - 2e nWoD game set in Philadelphia<br /> <a href=\"http://www.gravenlore.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Graven Lore</a> - 2e multi-venue nWoD game<br /> <a href=\"http://newhaven.mindrealms.com/\" target=\"_blank\">New Haven</a> - 2e nWoD game set in southern Maine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/951-caelene","name":"Caelene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar951_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T10:34:18-07:00","id":912302,"title":"","content":"Great start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T12:30:35-07:00","id":912378,"title":"","content":"I like the sound of this freehold, but I think it's better to wait a bit more for the release of 2ED. In the meantime, you can take a look at this <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/838042-2e-fan-update-to-oneirophysic-privilege\"><b>update of the Oneirophysics to 2ED</b></a> for ideas on privileges and how they are tied to an Entitlement's theme.","si